# Permissions

This file owns the access vocabulary and enforcement model for HOSSPI HMS.

## Vocabulary

- Core verbs are `view`, `create`, `edit`/`update`, `delete`, `manage`, `export`, `assign`, and `approve`.
- Module-specific verbs may be added when needed, such as `request`, `report`, `dispense`, or `prescribe`.
- `lab` and `radiology` use `request` and `report`; `pharmacy` uses `prescribe` and `dispense`.

## Access Model

- Permissions may attach to users, roles, modules, and subscription packages.
- Effective access = `union(role/module/user grants) ∩ subscription ∩ ABAC`.
- Users may hold multiple roles, but access must never exceed the active subscription or ABAC scope.

## ABAC

- Scope checks must consider tenant, facility, department, unit, ward, room, bed, ownership, assignment, and status.
- `own` and `assigned` should be preferred over broad `view all` or `manage all`.
- Every permission decision must be recordable and auditable.

## Enforcement

- UI, API, menu, component, and workflow access must all pass effective-access checks.
- Backend enforcement must remain authoritative over UI visibility.
- Permission changes and resets must be atomic, versioned, and auditable.
- Failed changes must roll back completely.

